    <title>Problems</title>
    <text><table><thead><tr><th>Problem</th><th>Clinical status</th><th>Verification</th><th>Code</th><th>Provenance</th></tr></thead><tbody>
  <tr ID="problem-1">
    <td>Bilateral gynecomastia, tender, about 4 cm of firm glandular tissue behind each nipple, after a year of high-dose estrogen; synthetic modern diagnosis linked to the documented breast growth from his hormone treatment</td><td>active</td><td>confirmed</td>
    <td>N62</td><td>S — Synthetic modern diagnosis. That the hormone treatment caused breast growth is reported in the sources (D, mentioned once in his own words); the examination findings are synthetic.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr ID="problem-2">
    <td>Suppressed testosterone and gonadotropins from exogenous estrogen (drug-induced hypogonadotropic hypogonadism), with low libido, erectile difficulty, and fatigue</td><td>resolved</td><td>confirmed</td>
    <td>E23.1</td><td>S — Synthetic consequence of high-dose estrogen, which suppresses LH and FSH; recovery is expected once it stops.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr ID="problem-3">
    <td>Adverse effects of high-dose estrogen given for a year without free and informed consent, as the alternative to imprisonment</td><td>active</td><td>confirmed</td>
    <td>T38.5X5A</td><td>S — Synthetic modern framing of the documented hormone treatment imposed after his conviction (D); in the modern episode it is recorded as iatrogenic harm.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr ID="problem-4">
    <td>Major depressive disorder, single episode, moderate, after prosecution and coerced hormone treatment; synthetic modern diagnosis (no depression diagnosis is documented in his lifetime)</td><td>active</td><td>confirmed</td>
    <td>F32.1</td><td>S — Synthetic modern diagnosis. That he sought Jungian analysis after the trial is documented (D); calling his state then a depressive illness is a retrospective interpretation (R).</td>
  </tr>
  <tr ID="problem-5">
    <td>Vitamin D insufficiency (25-hydroxyvitamin D 22 ng/mL)</td><td>resolved</td><td>confirmed</td>
    <td>E55.9</td><td>S — Synthetic finding of the bone-health workup.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr ID="problem-6">
    <td>Right lateral ankle sprain while trail running, able to bear weight, Ottawa ankle rules negative; resolved</td><td>active</td><td>confirmed</td>
    <td>S93.401A</td><td>S — Synthetic sprain at an unscheduled visit, chosen to teach the Ottawa ankle rules and how to protect a depression plan that relies on running; it does not echo any documented injury.</td>
  </tr></tbody></table></text>

